            "text": "{\"businessDate\":\"2025-07-23\",\"showtimes\":[{\"id\":\"KIN1-18787\",\"schedule\":{\"businessDate\":\"2025-07-23\",\"startsAt\":\"2025-07-23T18:00:00+01:00\",\"endsAt\":\"2025-07-23T20:13:00+01:00\",\"filmStartsAt\":\"2025-07-23T18:25:00+01:00\",\"filmEndsAt\":\"2025-07-23T20:13:00+01:00\",\"inSeatItemDelivery\":null},\"isSoldOut\":false,\"seatLayoutId\":\"KIN1-2-7\",\"filmId\":\"HO00001704\",\"siteId\":\"KIN1\",\"screenId\":\"KIN1-2\",\"areaCategories\":[{\"areaCategoryId\":\"KIN1-0000000001\",\"isAllocatedSeating\":true}],\"attributeIds\":[\"0000000053\"],\"isAllocatedSeating\":true,\"requires3dGlasses\":false,\"eventId\":null,\"restrictions\":[\"FilmAdvanceBookingRule\"],\"filmAdvanceBookingRuleId\":\"KIN1-6-HO00001704\"}],\"relatedData\":{\"sites\":[{\"id\":\"KIN1\",\"name\":{\"text\":\"Kingston\",\"translations\":[]},\"location\":{\"latitude\":51.412,\"longitude\":-0.3046},\"contactDetails\":{\"phoneNumbers\":[],\"email\":\"\",\"address\":{\"line1\":\"The Bentall Centre,\",\"line2\":\"London,\",\"city\":\"KT1 1TP\"}},\"ianaTimeZoneName\":\"Europe/London\"}],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"HO00001704\",\"title\":{\"text\":\"Film Club: Happy End\",\"translations\":[]},\"synopsis\":{\"text\":\"Master auteur Michael Haneke (Amour, The White Ribbon, Hidden) returns with a biting satire on bourgeois family values set in the shadow of the European refugee crisis. Featuring a cast of top acting talent, including Isabelle Huppert, Jean-Louis Trintignant, Mathieu Kassovitz and Toby Jones, it’s a piercing dark comedy on the blind preoccupations of middle-class angst.\\n\\nWhen her mother falls ill under mysterious circumstances, young Eve (Fantine Harduin) is sent to live with her estranged father’s relatives in Calais. The Laurent family – wealthy, neurotic and self-obsessed – own a lucrative construction company and live in a sprawling mansion house, waited on by servants. But trouble is brewing, as a series of intergenerational back-stabbings threaten to tear the family apart. Meanwhile, distracted by infidelities and betrayals, they fail to notice that their new arrival has a sinister secret of her own.\\n\\nNominated for the Palme d’Or at the 2017 Cannes Film Festival, Happy End bears all the hallmarks of Haneke’s uniquely stark and unsympathetic style. Pairing pitch-black humour with chillingly precise direction, it’s proof – if we ever needed it – that he remains one of modern cinema’s true visionaries.\",\"translations\":[]},\"shortSynopsis\":{\"text\":\"A drama about a family set in Calais with the European refugee crisis as the backdrop.\",\"translations\":[]},\"censorRatingId\":\"HO00000006\",\"censorRatingNote\":{\"text\":\"strong sex references, suicide references, language\",\"translations\":[]},\"releaseDate\":\"2025-08-23\",\"runtimeInMinutes\":108,\"trailerUrl\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_n_yk2AT7w\",\"displayPriority\":50,\"castAndCrew\":[{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000000258\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000000491\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000002163\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000010826\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000011334\",\"roles\":[\"Director\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000011335\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000011336\",\"roles\":[\"Producer\"]}],\"genreIds\":[\"0000000002\"],\"externalIds\":{\"moviexchangeReleaseId\":null,\"corporateId\":null},\"hopk\":\"HO00001704\",\"hoCode\":\"A000002184\",\"eventId\":null,\"distributorName\":\"Curzon\"}],\"castAndCrew\":[{\"id\":\"0000000258\",\"name\":{\"givenName\":\"Isabelle\",\"familyName\":\"Huppert\",\"middleName\":null}},{\"id\":\"0000000491\",\"name\":{\"givenName\":\"Franz \",\"familyName\":\"Rogowski\",\"middleName\":null}},{\"id\":\"0000002163\",\"name\":{\"givenName\":\"Toby\",\"familyName\":\"Jones\",\"middleName\":null}},{\"id\":\"0000010826\",\"name\":{\"givenName\":\"Jean-Louis\",\"familyName\":\"Trintignant\